Xyce 7.10: call std::abs(val), not std::abs<double>(val).

std::abs for floating point is not a template, so the explicit template
argument only resolved against libc++'s templated integer overloads.
Apple clang 21 / current libc++: "error: call to 'abs' is ambiguous".
Upstream Xyce master makes the same change.

